1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,834
One wrong room and the hunt is over.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:07,519
Hunt the Wumpus, AI Edition remakes it in Unity:

3
00:00:07,519 --> 00:00:09,998
a hazard starts a trivia duel,

4
00:00:09,998 --> 00:00:12,891
and a language model writes the question.

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,921
The map warns, Bats nearby.

6
00:00:15,921 --> 00:00:19,559
Then a pit drops the player into three trivia

7
00:00:19,559 --> 00:00:21,580
questions, the only way out.

8
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:25,200
Final question, then back to the map:

9
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,857
I feel a breeze,

10
00:00:26,857 --> 00:00:28,099
a pit nearby.

11
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,699
Colour describes your room.

12
00:00:30,699 --> 00:00:32,599
Text describes the neighbours.

13
00:00:32,599 --> 00:00:36,872
From those clues, you deduce where the Wumpus hides.

14
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:41,585
A language model writes each question on the spot.

15
00:00:41,585 --> 00:00:43,356
If the API fails,

16
00:00:43,356 --> 00:00:46,456
an offline bank keeps the game playable.

17
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:51,745
Try it at github.com/Mallard64/Wumpus
